  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Confirm the r1 gate and 020; read the list/get/preview/open-link handlers and decide whether an extraction is needed (note it).</step>
    <step order="2">If needed, write the frozen-bytes test, then extract.</step>
    <step order="3">Write the two tools and ledger rows; write the contract and not-found tests; run MCP suites, ArchTests and conformance.</step>
    <step order="4">Measure the publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="5">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="6">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the REST routes answer 403 vs 404 differently for forbidden vs missing and a uniform tool result would contradict a documented contract, STOP and escalate (uac-r2).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>notes/reuse-scan.md rows "Document list" and "Document preview/open links": DataverseDocumentsEndpoints ListDocumentsAsync, FileAccessEndpoints preview-url/open-links over IDocumentDataverseService and SPE; CAPABILITY-INDEX document-access row.</existing>
    <extension>The route logic is reused (extracted to a shared method only if it is inline); the tools are thin adapters on r1's host.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Copilot users cannot list or open matter documents, and the email widget (011/040) has no attachment source (FR-03, FR-12 fail).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">dotnet build; dotnet test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Documents/ListDocumentsTool.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Documents/GetDocumentTool.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Api/Mcp/Documents/DocumentToolsContractTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/auth/Mcp/Documents/DocumentToolsNotFoundTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">For an allowed document, get returns the REST metadata and the same preview/open links; list by regarding matter returns the REST ids.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a forbidden document and a non-existent id return byte-identical isError not-found results.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no caller context returns UserContextRequired.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">If an extraction happened, the REST frozen-bytes test passes before and after.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Results under 64 KiB at the list maximum; ArchTests and conformance pass; publish-size delta recorded; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-03. uac-r2 reviews. Done 2026-11-25 on a wave worktree (not merged): decisions in notes/023-decisions.md; deferred D-023-1/2 in notes/defer-issues.md; capability-index row pending in notes/capability-index-pending.md. TASK-INDEX.md not edited (wave rule; main session). rework: none task 023</notes>

